1488	 * randomized path, served by the account's own PHP-FPM socket via the existing
1489	 * vhost (a non-dot directory, so the vhost's `location ~ /\.` deny rule doesn't
1490	 * shadow it, and it survives the SSL/health vhost reinstalls — no per-account
1491	 * `location` block that a self-heal could wipe).
1492	 *
1493	 * SECURITY: this is NOT an unauthenticated, root-logged-in phpMyAdmin. Adminer
1494	 * shows only a LOGIN form; the customer authenticates with their OWN scoped DB
1495	 * user (created by createHostingDatabase / buildScopedGrantSql — granted on THAT
1496	 * customer's databases only, '<user>'@'localhost'). So even if the randomized URL
1497	 * leaks: (1) the visitor still needs a valid DB username+password, which only the
1498	 * tenant knows; (2) MySQL only accepts those creds from localhost — Adminer runs
1499	 * inside the tenant's own FPM pool on the node, so the connection is localhost;
1500	 * (3) the grants confine that user to its own databases, so there is no lateral
1501	 * path to a neighbour's data. The file is downloaded AS the jailed account user
1502	 * (never root), so it lands owned by the tenant inside their chroot.
1503	 */
